WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.585 --> 00:00:04.880
It was one of the last tours
of Hot Fuss.

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:07.132
We'd been writing songs
during sound checks.

00:00:09.927 --> 00:00:11.845
There was so much need
on our part

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:13.680
to get another record going.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.936
There were some chords
that were floating around

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.229
from months before.

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.690
A lot of ideas are created
off just a chord progression

00:00:23.774 --> 00:00:25.984
that you try
and do something with

00:00:26.068 --> 00:00:27.402
and it evolves from there.

00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:30.697
That one was
almost accidental.

00:00:30.781 --> 00:00:33.367
Towards the end
of a practice.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.535
Towards the end
of the night…

00:00:34.618 --> 00:00:37.829
Mark was playing around
with a bass line.

00:00:40.999 --> 00:00:43.335
Dave suggested we go up.
He added a note.

00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:45.295
So a three-note riff became
a four-note riff

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:46.922
because of something
he suggested.

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:49.258
He was messing around
with these three chords.

00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:52.553
I was like: "Oh! Add these
two and then go back to it."

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:57.266
It was
those first three chords

00:00:57.349 --> 00:01:00.269
that just, you know,
awakened us.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:15.033
To have four people be
so in tune

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:17.911
and be able to tap into
the universe

00:01:17.995 --> 00:01:20.789
for a second is magic,
you know.

00:01:20.873 --> 00:01:22.040
And we're really lucky,
I think,

00:01:22.124 --> 00:01:24.459
you know, to have had that
happen at all.

00:01:25.169 --> 00:01:27.254
It was just nice to know
that you had something good

00:01:27.337 --> 00:01:28.297
that you could get behind,

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.381
but the labour came.

00:01:32.384 --> 00:01:34.970
At what point do you start
coming up with lyrics?

00:01:35.679 --> 00:01:37.556
This is another one
of those strange moments

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:39.516
where I have a lot
come to me right away.

00:01:40.142 --> 00:01:42.102
"He doesn't look
a thing like Jesus,

00:01:42.186 --> 00:01:43.353
but he talks
like a gentleman

00:01:43.437 --> 00:01:44.730
like you imagine
when you were young."

00:01:44.813 --> 00:01:45.814
That was the first day.

00:01:45.898 --> 00:01:49.651
He doesn't look
a thing like Jesus

00:01:49.735 --> 00:01:52.029
but he talks
like a gentleman

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:57.701
like you imagine
when you were young

00:01:58.243 --> 00:02:00.204
That made it a lot easier
to write around

00:02:00.287 --> 00:02:03.665
because I had something
foundational there.

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.544
It helped, I think,

00:02:09.004 --> 00:02:10.923
direct me for
the rest of the record, too.

00:02:12.508 --> 00:02:15.511
Your ears pricked
by the word "Jesus"

00:02:15.594 --> 00:02:18.639
and then you get the
delivery of the guitar riff.

00:02:18.722 --> 00:02:21.975
It sort of fulfils a lot of
different emotions.

00:02:22.059 --> 00:02:24.019
-It's not obvious.
-No.

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:25.729
And that's what makes
the track brilliant.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:28.941
Can we climb this mountain?
I don't know

00:02:29.441 --> 00:02:32.653
Higher now than ever before

00:02:32.736 --> 00:02:36.782
I know we can make it
if we take it slow

00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:39.952
Let's take it easy
Easy now, watch it go

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:44.414
I knew there was
some kind of redemption

00:02:44.498 --> 00:02:46.124
that was going to be
a thread.

00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:47.292
I think it had to do with

00:02:47.376 --> 00:02:48.502
things that I was going
through.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:54.091
Excess and debauchery
in rock and roll, you know,

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:57.928
had been sort of glorified
and glamourised for so long.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:03:00.389
You know, we sort of
got thrust into it.

00:03:01.056 --> 00:03:02.933
And I realised right away
that that wasn't for me.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:06.353
One of the things that I
also got in the stands

00:03:06.436 --> 00:03:07.813
is a piece of the song that

00:03:07.896 --> 00:03:08.897
I don't think is
in the song.

00:03:08.981 --> 00:03:10.232
This part.

00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:14.194
-Higher, higher
-Yeah!

00:03:14.278 --> 00:03:15.237
There's another…

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.364
Ok, we took ass
at that lyric.

00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:19.658
This is, again, where Flood
and Moulder were crucial.

00:03:19.741 --> 00:03:21.702
You know, you need people
to tell you no.

00:03:22.286 --> 00:03:24.705
There we go! Saved it from…

00:03:24.788 --> 00:03:27.583
loitering
in the bargain bins.

00:03:27.666 --> 00:03:30.043
Higher, higher

00:03:30.127 --> 00:03:34.464
I said he doesn't look
a thing like Jesus

00:03:34.965 --> 00:03:37.801
Thank heavens that didn't
make it onto the final mix.

00:03:37.885 --> 00:03:39.845
I'd forgotten about it
until just now.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:43.599
How'd that get sent to you?

00:03:43.682 --> 00:03:44.725
Yeah, why do you have that?

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.477
Take his laptop, now.

